1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:03,251
Shh…

2
00:00:03,301 --> 00:00:05,930
This cave hides huge halls under the mountain,

3
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:08,375
and stone spikes hanging from the ceiling…

4
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:09,823
but who carved all this?

5
00:00:10,642 --> 00:00:11,372
Drip, drip…

6
00:00:11,422 --> 00:00:13,714
one drop falls every ten seconds.

7
00:00:13,764 --> 00:00:14,849
And Noah laughs:

8
00:00:14,899 --> 00:00:17,475
that's not going to carve a mountain!

9
00:00:17,525 --> 00:00:18,093
And yet…

10
00:00:18,872 --> 00:00:20,386
Discovery mission!

11
00:00:22,902 --> 00:00:23,464
Mini mode!

12
00:00:23,514 --> 00:00:25,730
Passing through the air and the soil,

13
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:27,813
rainwater picks up carbon dioxide…

14
00:00:27,863 --> 00:00:29,650
so it becomes a little acidic,

15
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:31,109
like a sugar-free soda.

16
00:00:31,892 --> 00:00:34,584
This water slips into cracks in the limestone,

17
00:00:34,634 --> 00:00:36,491
a rock it knows how to dissolve.

18
00:00:36,541 --> 00:00:38,518
Drop after drop, the crack widens…

19
00:00:38,568 --> 00:00:40,297
into a corridor, then a hall!

20
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:41,982
And the stone spikes?

21
00:00:42,032 --> 00:00:46,428
The water reaches the cave loaded with limestone, loses its gas, and the limestone settles back:

22
00:00:46,478 --> 00:00:49,765
a stalactite grows from the ceiling, a stalagmite rises from the floor.

23
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:52,377
Natural chalk is limestone.

24
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:53,984
So in vinegar, an acid,

25
00:00:54,034 --> 00:00:55,731
it melts away in bubbles!

26
00:00:55,781 --> 00:00:58,716
Rainwater does the same, only more slowly.

27
00:00:59,491 --> 00:01:01,521
And that's how caves are carved out.

28
00:01:03,022 --> 00:01:06,950
Rainwater, slightly acidic, dissolves limestone drop by drop:

29
00:01:06,1000 --> 00:01:09,087
millions of years later, a cave.

30
00:01:09,925 --> 00:01:10,732
With an adult:

31
00:01:10,782 --> 00:01:13,487
put a piece of natural chalk in some vinegar…

32
00:01:13,537 --> 00:01:14,527
it makes bubbles!

33
00:01:14,577 --> 00:01:16,964
And the next day, the chalk has shrunk!

34
00:01:17,752 --> 00:01:18,910
And why does the sky

35
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:20,723
light up green near the poles?

36
00:01:20,773 --> 00:01:21,981
The answer tomorrow.
